-{"id": "orch-g8c.3", "title": "MVP supervisor loop: multi-agent multi-worktree convergence runner", "description": "Run a reconciliation loop over active beads and ai_orch sessions. For each bead/session, evaluate tmux liveness, PR presence, CI status, and review blockers; then decide continue/retry/done/needs_human and emit notifications.", "notes": "Implement minimal supervisor/monitor loop for multi-agent multi-worktree sessions.\nAdded registry-based supervisor reconciliation path: missing session => mapping transitions to needs_human + task_needs_human loopback event emitted.\n2026-03-07: Two concrete deliverables identified: (1) Hermes dispatch skill in hermes-config/ that writes BeadSessionMapping with slack_trigger_ts at spawn time. (2) launchd plist or supervisor entry point running reconcile_registry_once on schedule. These are the only blockers for the full 3-step Slack loop.\n2026-03-07: Built both deliverables. dispatch_task.py: CLI Hermes calls to spawn ai_orch + write BeadSessionMapping with slack_trigger_ts. supervisor.py: persistent daemon loop (SIGTERM-safe, --once mode for testing). hermes-config/skills/dispatch-task/SKILL.md: step-by-step Hermes dispatch instructions. launchd plist+install script. Remaining: install supervisor (scripts/install-mctrl-supervisor.sh) and read dispatch skill into hermes SOUL/skills config.\n2026-03-07: All deliverables tested and verified via ralph.sh. Supervisor daemon installed as ai.mctrl.supervisor launchd agent (PID 2780, running). SUP-1: --once clean exit. SUP-2: dead session → task_needs_human. SUP-3: ai_orch output parsing. SUP-4: launchd install. SUP-5: 476 tests pass. Ready to close pending Hermes reading dispatch-task SKILL.md.", "status": "in_progress", "priority": 1, "issue_type": "feature", "owner": "jleechan@example.com", "created_at": "2026-03-05T17:31:18Z", "created_by": "jleechan", "updated_at": "2026-03-07T10:05:12Z", "source_repo": ".", "compaction_level": 0, "original_size": 0, "labels": ["conve