-{"id":"orch-cbo6","title":"Design webhook-first PR comment/CI remediation loop for Symphony","description":"Define a durable architecture to replace cron-only PR polling with GitHub webhook ingestion, idempotent event processing, and a Symphony execution worker. Scope includes event contract, dedupe strategy, retry/escalation policy, and migration plan from current hermes cron polling.","design":"Primary trigger must be GitHub App webhooks (issue_comment, pull_request_review_comment, check_run/check_suite, workflow_run). Event ingress should ACK quickly, persist raw payload + delivery ID, and enqueue for async processing. Worker invokes sym-dispatch using bounded retries and max-fix-attempt budget; reconciler cron remains as safety net for missed/stuck events. Include observability and SLOs for queue lag, retry counts, and PR convergence latency.","acceptance_criteria":"Roadmap document under roadmap/ defines architecture, state machine, event schema, failure handling, rollout plan, and operator runbook. Design explicitly calls out why webhook-first is required and what cron is retained for. Follow-up implementation beads can be created directly from this design.","status":"open","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","owner":"jleechan@example.com","created_at":"2026-03-13T05:12:23Z","created_by":"jleechan","updated_at":"2026-03-13T05:12:23Z","source_repo":".","compaction_level":0,"original_size":0,"dependencies":[{"issue_id":"orch-cbo6","depends_on_id":"orch-cbo","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-03-12T22:12:23Z","created_by":"jleechan","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""}]}
-{"id":"orch-cbo61","title":"Webhook ingress service + signature validation","description":"Implement a GitHub App webhook ingress endpoint for PR remediation events. Scope includes receiving webhook deliveries, validating X-Hub-Signature-256, storing raw payload + headers + receive timestamp, and fast ACK before async processing.","design":"Ingress must be idempotent on delivery ID and fail-closed on signature mismatch. Persist canonical metadata needed for replay and troubleshooting. Keep handler lightweight; enqueue normalized work and return immediately.","acceptance_criteria":"Webhook endpoint validates signatures correctly, records delivery IDs with payload metadata, rejects invalid signatures, and enqueues valid events for async processing. Includes tests for valid/invalid signatures and duplicate delivery handling.","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","owner":"jleechan@example.com","created_at":"2026-03-13T08:11:31Z","created_by":"jleechan","updated_at":"2026-03-13T08:11:31Z","closed_at":"2026-03-13T08:11:31Z","close_reason":"Implemented","source_repo":".","compaction_level":0,"original_size":0,"dependencies":[{"issue_id":"orch-cbo61","depends_on_id":"orch-cbo6","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-03-13T01:11:31Z","created_by":"jleechan","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""}]}
-{"id":"orch-cbo62","title":"Event normalizer, dedupe keys, and queue schema","description":"Define and implement event normalization for webhook payloads into a stable remediation queue contract. Include dedupe key generation, stale head-SHA handling, and queue persistence schema for retries and replay.","design":"Normalized key should include repo, PR number, signal type, signal ID, and head SHA. Drop exact duplicate deliveries, suppress stale signals for older head SHAs unless replay-required, and emit canonical queue records with attempt counters and next-attempt timestamps.","acceptance_criteria":"Queue schema and normalizer are implemented with deterministic keying and tests covering duplicate deliveries, stale SHA suppression, and valid event normalization across issue_comment/review/check events.","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","owner":"jleechan@example.com","created_at":"2026-03-13T08:11:37Z","created_by":"jleechan","updated_at":"2026-03-13T08:11:37Z","closed_at":"2026-03-13T08:11:37Z","close_reason":"Implemented","source_repo":".","compaction_level":0,"original_size":0,"dependencies":[{"issue_id":"orch-cbo62","depends_on_id":"orch-cbo6","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-03-13T01:11:37Z","created_by":"jleechan","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""}]}
-{"id":"orch-cbo63","title":"Symphony worker with PR lock + bounded retries","description":"Build the async remediation worker that consumes normalized queue events and executes Symphony dispatch for actionable PR signals. Add PR-level locking, attempt budgeting, and escalation when retry limits are exceeded.","design":"Worker must enforce one active remediation loop per repo+PR, generate deterministic task prompts, run sym-dispatch with explicit timeout, and record transition/audit events for each attempt. Retry policy should be bounded with exponential backoff and terminal escalation state.","acceptance_criteria":"Worker executes end-to-end remediation attempts from queue records, enforces PR lock semantics, honors retry/timeout budgets, and emits converged/escalated terminal states with tests for lock contention and retry exhaustion.","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","owner":"jleechan@example.com","created_at":"2026-03-13T08:11:47Z","created_by":"jleechan","updated_at":"2026-03-13T08:11:47Z","closed_at":"2026-03-13T08:11:47Z","close_reason":"Implemented","source_repo":".","compaction_level":0,"original_size":0,"dependencies":[{"issue_id":"orch-cbo63","depends_on_id":"orch-cbo6","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-03-13T01:11:46Z","created_by":"jleechan","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""}]}
-{"id":"orch-cbo64","title":"Reconciler cron + missed-delivery recovery","description":"Implement a reconciliation loop that audits webhook/queue/PR state for drift and recovers missed or stuck remediation events. This is the cron safety-net layer, not the primary trigger path.","design":"Reconciler should detect orphaned queue items, stale in-progress attempts, and missed webhook deliveries (via delivery status APIs/logs), then safely requeue with idempotent guards. Include runtime thresholds and safe backoff for repeated recovery failures.","acceptance_criteria":"Scheduled reconciler detects and repairs at least: missed delivery, orphaned queue item, and stuck in-progress worker state. Tests or deterministic simulations cover each recovery path and preserve idempotency.","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","owner":"jleechan@example.com","created_at":"2026-03-13T08:11:57Z","created_by":"jleechan","updated_at":"2026-03-13T08:11:57Z","closed_at":"2026-03-13T08:11:57Z","close_reason":"Implemented","source_repo":".","compaction_level":0,"original_size":0,"dependencies":[{"issue_id":"orch-cbo64","depends_on_id":"orch-cbo6","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-03-13T01:11:57Z","created_by":"jleechan","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""}]}
